<title>HUNGARY: Hungary three-month bill yield falls to 19.49 pct.</title>
<headline>Hungary three-month bill yield falls to 19.49 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average annual yield on the latest issue of three-month discount treasury bills was set by auction at 19.49 percent, down from 19.52 percent at an auction one week ago, the Government Debt Management Agency said.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow.</p>
<p>    Total on offer	     5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total bids received     15,843.71 million forints</p>
<p>    Total allocated	    5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Total issued		 5,000 million forints</p>
<p>    Average annual yield	    19.49 pct</p>
<p>    Average price		     95.3660 pct</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
